  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The zigzag – passing up the whole court",
  "description": "The players are spread out in a zigzag over the whole court, alternately left and right, with a starting line holding the balls at one end. The ball is passed up the court in a zigzag from player to player. Whoever has passed runs at full speed straight after it and takes the receiver's place.\n\nThe last player receives the ball, dribbles back along the boards and joins the back of the starting line. The next ball can go as soon as the first is a little way up. Raise the ball speed as you go and aim for one-touch passes. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Hard, accurate passes without bounces."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Run straight after the pass – at full speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Try to play first time: receive and pass in one movement."
    }
  ],
